        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
        ":question/problem": "Calculate the integral $\\int \\frac{3}{x\\log{\\left(6 x \\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let's set $u=\\log{\\left(6 x \\right)}.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{6 x}\\cdot 6=\\frac{1}{x}\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3}{x\\log{\\left(6 x \\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\int \\frac{1}{\\log{\\left(6 x \\right)}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{u^{-1}}{-1}+C \\\\  & =- \\frac{3}{u}+C \\\\  & =- \\frac{3}{\\log{\\left(6 x \\right)}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
